# ONNX Runtime pins. The one place they live.
#
# Read by scripts/fetch_ort.py (which downloads and extracts) and by
# core/openworld-core/build.rs (which builds the `library` digest for the
# target into the core, so the core refuses any other library bytes at load).
#
# Columns, separated by spaces:
#   platform  kind  sha256  name  member
#
#   wheel      The PyPI wheel. sha256 is the digest PyPI publishes for that file.
#              name is the wheel's file name; member is "-".
#   library    The library the core loads. sha256 is of the file inside that
#              wheel, computed from the wheel downloaded from PyPI and checked
#              against the wheel pin. name is the file name it is installed as;
#              member is its path inside the wheel.
#   companion  Another file extracted beside the library, checked by
#              fetch_ort.py only: a library ONNX Runtime loads itself, or
#              ONNX Runtime's license and notices, which ship with it.
#
# To move to a new ONNX Runtime: take each wheel's sha256 from PyPI, download
# the wheel, check it, hash the files inside it, and replace these lines. Never
# type a digest from memory.

